// =============================================================================
// CHANGELOG
// =============================================================================
//
// v6.12 (2026-09-10)
// -----------------
// Bridge: fix Firefox Xray "Permission denied" on evalPreflopHand
//   - The bridge's evalPreflopHand took an array of hole cards. Card Highlight (and the
//     diagnostics script) run @grant none, unprivileged page-context — their array is built
//     in that unprivileged realm, and Firefox's Xray wrappers can refuse this sandboxed
//     script permission to read a property on it, even .length, throwing "Permission denied
//     to access property" from inside evalPreflopHand's own first line. Arrays are exactly
//     the object shape this trips on; primitives cross the boundary fine.
//   - Fixed by adding evalPreflopHandBridge(card1, card2, position, facingRaise) — two plain
//     strings instead of an array — and pointing the bridge's evalPreflopHand property at
//     that wrapper instead of the raw internal function. The array gets built here, inside
//     this script's own realm, from primitives that already crossed safely. Internal callers
//     within this script are untouched; they still call evalPreflopHand(holeCards, ...)
//     directly. Bridge bumped to v3.1 — the property name is unchanged, only how many
//     arguments a caller passes.
//
// v6.10 (2026-09-10)
// -----------------
// Bridge: expose the preflop range evaluator for Card Highlight
//   - evalPreflopHand (position + facing-raise aware raise/call/fold read) and a new
//     getLivePreflopContext() (hero's live position and whether a preflop raise is already
//     in) are now on window.__tornPokerHUD_bridge, bumped to v3. Card Highlight's new range-
//     theme feature reads both instead of re-implementing position detection — one seat/
//     range brain shared by both scripts, so they can't disagree with each other.
//
// v6.9 (2026-09-03)
// -----------------
// Per-table stats key on the table, not the blind size
//   - byTable was keyed by handBB, so every table sharing a blind collapsed into one bucket.
//     Three tables run at 1M (River Wizard, Tripod, Comatose Cove), two at 5M and four at
//     100K, which meant the single largest stats bucket in a typical export was a blend of
//     tables with different player pools — and no stat could tell them apart.
//   - Buckets now key on the table's texture (river_wizard, comatose_cove, ...) via
//     resolveTableKey(), falling back to the blind size when the texture cannot be read, so a
//     hand at an unidentified table is still split by stake instead of being dropped.
//     getTableBucket() is the single accessor; every write site in hand finalization goes
//     through it rather than reaching into byTable directly.
//   - Existing data migrates in place on the first new hand at a table: a bucket left under a
//     bare blind is adopted by the named table when that blind belongs to exactly one table.
//     When several tables share it the old bucket is left alone and labelled "mixed" instead,
//     because those hands genuinely cannot be attributed after the fact. Nothing is discarded.
//   - History entries carry tableKey alongside bbAmount, so getActiveStats() can narrow to one
//     table exactly; entries written before this version still match on their blind.
//   - A texture is only trusted when its blind matches the hand's, which discards a key left
//     over from a previous table after a switch the texture reader missed. The blind-only
//     fallback path in the table-change handler clears the stale texture for the same reason.
//   - Cross-device merge: the new per-bucket bb field is carried, not summed, or two devices
//     reporting the same table would double its blind size.
//
// Hero P&L per table, in big blinds
//   - Each bucket now records the owner's own result at that table: heroNetChips, heroNetBB and
//     heroPnlHands, written from the same net figure that already feeds the session counters.
//   - The Tables tab shows net BB and BB/100 first and cash after it, dimmed. Cash rewards
//     blind size rather than how well a table was played, so ranking tables by it points at
//     whichever stake is largest — +$531m at a 25M table is 21 BB.
//
// v6.8 (2026-08-31)
// -----------------
// TornPDA: net worth and faction tags never worked
//   - tornApiFetch() had its own transport ladder with no TornPDA branch: it checked for
//     GM_xmlhttpRequest, and TornPDA does not define that unless the user separately installs
//     the GMforPDA shim, so it fell through to native fetch() — which the app's webview blocks
//     cross-origin. The request never left the page, and both callers only ever saw a generic
//     failure, which is why this looked like an API key problem rather than a transport one.
//   - Now built on gmRequest(), which already had the bridge, so there is one transport for
//     every network call in the script. gmRequest additionally prefers TornPDA's documented
//     globals (PDA_httpGet/Post/Put/Patch/Delete) over calling the handler directly, because
//     each one awaits __PDA_platformReadyPromise — a request fired before the app bridge is
//     wired up now waits instead of failing. Raw callHandler stays as the fallback.
//   - Torn API error bodies are logged with their code instead of being swallowed.
//
// TornPDA: an empty injected key counted as a key
//   - TornPDA substitutes ###PDA-APIKEY### unconditionally (a plain replaceAll in
//     userscripts_provider.adaptSource), using the script's own custom key if set and the
//     app's main key otherwise — and an EMPTY string when the user has no key configured at
//     all. HAS_PDA_KEY only tested whether the sentinel had changed, so an empty substitution
//     read as "key injected": every API lookup then bailed out silently while Settings
//     claimed the key was handled automatically. Now also requires a plausible key length.
//
// TornPDA: the API key field was unreachable
//   - The settings UI hid the key input behind isPDA(), which is true whenever the Flutter
//     webview is present — but the key is only substituted when the user has granted this
//     script API access in TornPDA. Without that grant the user was shown "API key is
//     injected automatically, no action needed" above a field that did not exist, with no
//     way to supply a key. Both the input and the save handler now key off HAS_PDA_KEY (was
//     the key actually substituted), and PDA users without the grant get an explicit note.
//
// Stats disappearing on TornPDA
//   - Inside TornPDA the script's IndexedDB is ordinary webview storage: Android can evict it
//     under storage pressure, and clearing the app's browser cache deletes it outright.
//     Nothing in the script was deleting anyone's stats; the platform was.
//   - IndexedDB stays the primary store on every platform. It was tempting to move wholesale
//     to TornPDA's PDA_storage (app-owned SQLite, survives a cache clear), but that is capped
//     at 50 MB per script — 10 MB by default — and a long-lived store runs past that, so it
//     could only have become primary by discarding tracked players or hand history.
//   - Instead the native store holds a backup written alongside the real one. Under 8 MB the
//     whole store is backed up verbatim, which covers most players outright. Past that it
//     falls back to a seed: every tracked player's counters and shown hands with the heavy
//     per-hand arrays dropped, which measures ~7 MB against a 65 MB store and so still fits
//     the default quota with no action from the user.
//   - On load, a primary store that comes back empty is repopulated from that backup and
//     written straight back, so a wipe costs hand history and per-stake splits instead of
//     every profile. Seed writes are throttled to 2 min — it needs to be present and roughly
//     current, not up to the last hand, and each one crosses the app bridge.
//   - navigator.storage.persist() is requested at init, which asks the engine to exempt the
//     origin from automatic eviction. It does nothing against a deliberate cache clear (that
//     is what the backup is for) but it addresses the other way storage goes missing.
//   - _openIDB() no longer memoizes a rejected open. A transient failure (webview still
//     starting, database briefly locked) used to leave every read and write for the rest of
//     the session silently no-opping against a database that would have opened on retry.
//   - New Storage section in Settings: primary store size, backup size against its quota, and
//     a specific warning when a save failed, the backup will not fit, or TornPDA is running
//     without native storage. Previously the first sign of trouble was an empty HUD — and as
//     of TornPDA 3.16.0 the app's own capacity warnings only appear with debug enabled.
//   - Save debounce goes 1.5s -> 4s on TornPDA. Still force-flushed on hide/unload.
//   - Note for TornPDA users: the backup is keyed to the script's storageId, a UUID assigned
//     when the script is added. Update in place; deleting and re-adding the script orphans it.
//
// v6.7 (2026-08-31)
// -----------------
// The line read now drives the advice, not just a panel beside it
//   - v6.6 put the line intelligence in a dossier block under the advice. The advice
//     sentence itself was still archetype-driven: oppRangeNote branched on the player's
//     type label ("Snake is a Sharp player — they pick spots") and that string is appended
//     to roughly 120 advice branches. A lifetime label describes a player across every hand
//     they have ever played; it says nothing about the line actually in front of you.
//   - getLineReadNote() compresses the line-conditioned tier mix into one sentence for the
//     advice text, falling back to the street-level bet composition when the exact line is
//     still thin, and returning null when neither clears its floor. Same spot, same board,
//     same archetype now reads differently depending on what the line has contained:
//       "…nothing 8, two pair 3. This line is a stab more often than a value bet, so do not
//        fold a decent hand to it on sizing alone."
//       "…nothing 2, a set or better 9. The top of their range runs this line, so a bluff
//        catcher is not enough here."
//   - Appended in buildSelfEntry rather than inside getOwnHandLean: only some of that
//     function's branches interpolate oppStr, and the read has to reach all of them. The
//     archetype note stands down entirely when a line read exists, so the two never stack.
//     With no line data the old archetype sentence is unchanged.
//
// Reconciling the line read with the hand-strength verdict
//   - The two come from different evidence and can point opposite ways. Printed side by
//     side that reads as the coach contradicting itself, so reconcileLineWithVerdict()
//     names the disagreement and gives a direction, using the verdict flags _setVerdict()
//     already records per branch.
//   - Runs after the equity pass, because "they bluff a lot" is not on its own a reason to
//     call — you still have to beat a bluff at showdown. With 12% equity against a 33%
//     price it says "raise or fold, do not call"; with 41% against the same price it says
//     call; with no equity number it stays conditional.
//
// Barrel read on the attack side
//   - When nobody has bet, the advice now carries how often this player gives up the next
//     street after what they just did. Deciding whether to fire turns on that number and
//     the coach only ever knew their flat fold-to-c-bet rate.
//
// - Dossier rows that the advice above already made are dropped rather than printed twice
//   (_sharesLongRun spots the shared counts fragment across the two different phrasings).
//
// v6.6 (2026-08-31)
// -----------------
// Two pair split out from "2 pair or better" everywhere
//   - Every shown-hand read used one "strong (2pr+)" bucket that averaged two pair together
//     with sets, straights, flushes and boats. Those get played as different hands — two
//     pair gets pot-controlled, bluff-caught with or folded to a scare card, a set gets
//     jammed or trapped with — so the bucket was averaging away the exact difference the
//     sizing and line reads exist to find. A player betting 40% of pot with two pair and
//     110% with a set read as "about 75% of pot with a real hand", which is nobody's
//     actual sizing.
//   - New shared HAND_TIERS ladder (air / one pair / two pair / set or better) plus
//     tierFromRank, newTierCounts, sumTiers, describeTierCounts and entryStreetBreakdown.
//     VALUE_TIER_KEYS keeps the value-vs-bluff binary available where a read genuinely
//     wants one, so nothing that needed the old grouping lost it.
//   - The Quick Read line history, the coach's line notes and the analyzer's strength
//     matrix, river-size buckets, sizing shapes and signature lines all read off it. The
//     analyzer imports the ladder over the bridge instead of defining its own, so a report
//     and the live coach can no longer disagree about what a bet contained.
//   - Reads that come out of the split, e.g. "his sizing splits the two: about 110% of pot
//     with a set or better against 40% with two pair — this one is 40%, which sits with the
//     two pairs", and "he bets 100% of his sets on the turn but only 45% of his two pairs,
//     so a check there is more often two pair than nothing".
//
// Coach panel: the deep read is now in the panel, not behind a button
//   - v6.3 built buildLiveActionRead() — line history, bluff profile, board fit, likely
//     holdings — and put all of it behind the ⚡ Quick Read button. The coach panel itself
//     kept showing one capped verdict line, which is why it read as surface level: the
//     reads existed, they were just never placed where they would be seen.
//   - buildCoachDossier() renders those reads inline. The self-entry carries a full dossier
//     on whoever is applying the pressure (or, in a checked pot, the live villain you know
//     most about who has acted); each acting opponent's own entry carries the line rows for
//     that player. The same read never prints twice — the opponent entries skip whoever the
//     self-entry already covered.
//   - Nothing is dropped to fit. Rows past the detail cap collapse behind a "+N more reads"
//     link in place rather than being discarded.
//
// Three analyzer cross-tabs brought forward into live play
//   - getStreetTierRead / buildStreetTierNotes: what they actually held the times they bet
//     this street, and how big they sized each tier, with the bet currently on the table
//     placed inside their own pattern. Wider sample than the line-conditioned read, so it
//     covers the spots where the exact line has only been seen once or twice — and it
//     suppresses its own composition rows when the line read already said the same thing
//     off the same hands.
//   - getContinuationDecay / buildContinuationDecayNote: how often they give up the next
//     street after this one's action. "He called the flop 15 times and folded the turn on
//     10 of them" is the number that decides a barrel, and the HUD never had it.
//   - getSizingShapeRead / buildSizingShapeNote: whether the shape of their sizing across
//     this hand (building, flat, fading, overbet jump) has meant value or air for them.
//   - Survivorship caveat added to the line read: cards only surface on hands that reached
//     showdown, so a line they fold half the time used to read far stronger than it is.
//
// Coach detail level
//   - New "Detail level" setting (full / normal / lean, full by default) replacing three
//     hardcoded caps: hudExtras was fixed at the top 2 notes and only one guaranteed tell
//     ever rendered no matter how many cleared their sample floor. Full shows every read
//     that clears its floor; lean restores something close to the old behaviour.
//   - Routine actions the low-signal gate had reduced to a one-liner are opened back up
//     when there is a real line read to attach, so a quiet call with 15 hands of history
//     behind it stops looking identical to one with none.
//   - "Inline player read" setting turns the whole dossier off for anyone who wants the
//     panel back the way it was.
//   - buildLiveActionRead is memoized per player per hand state — the coach re-renders
//     every logged action on each update, and the read walks a player's whole history.
//
// Villain pronouns in the live reads
//   - The Quick Read / dossier copy said "he" throughout for opponents whose gender the
//     script has no way of knowing. Switched to they/them across the strings that render
//     in that block (line history, street range, decay, sizing shape, board fit, bluff
//     profile, aggression shift) so one block reads consistently. _describeLine now
//     produces base-form verbs ("raise preflop, bet the flop") to agree with it. The rest
//     of the coach's copy is untouched and still says "he".
//
// v6.5 (2026-08-11)
// -----------------
// Per-hand blind size was lost in big-blind display mode
//   - The "posted big blind" handler read the amount with a $-only regex, so in BB view
//     ("posted big blind 1 BB") currentHand.bbAmount stayed null for every hand. That fed
//     potBB, the big-pot auto-pin threshold, the per-stake history filter and the tilt
//     card's big-loss test, all of which silently treated those hands as having no stake.
//   - Now goes through parseCashAmt, which already reads both formats. Converting the BB
//     form needs the table's stake, so the table is identified from the felt first when it
//     isn't known yet.
//
// Table blind size broadcast to other scripts
//   - New tphud:tableInfo event carrying { bb, name }, fired whenever the table context
//     changes, plus a tphud:requestTableInfo listener that replies on demand so a script
//     loading after the table was identified can pull the value instead of waiting.
//   - tphud:betHint now carries bb as well, so a listener that missed the broadcast still
//     learns the blind size.
//   - poker-bet-sizing.user.js uses this to size bets while Torn displays amounts in big
//     blinds: a "12.5 BB" pot can't become a cash bet without knowing what a blind is worth.
//     It reads the felt texture itself as its primary source and treats this as an override,
//     since the two scripts hold different @grant levels and events between them are not
//     guaranteed to cross the userscript sandbox boundary.
//
// Exact seat positions (display)
//   - getExactPosition() names the actual seat — BTN, SB, BB, UTG, UTG+1.., LJ, HJ, CO —
//     instead of only the EP/MP/LP bucket. Short tables drop the names they have no seats
//     for, so 6-handed reads UTG/HJ/CO and 4-handed reads UTG with no CO at all.
//   - Both it and getPlayerPosition now read one shared getSeatGeometry(). The exact label
//     excludes sitting-out seats (one phantom seat renames every middle position); the
//     coarse bucket deliberately does not, so no betting decision changes.
//   - Surfaces in coach sentences ("Raise from the hijack"), history cards, the Vs Me tab,
//     hand-copy output and showdown verdict reasons. Stats stay keyed on the coarse bucket.
//
// Small blind steal spot in the preflop coach
//   - Marginal hands folded around to you in the SB now get a raise/steal line instead of a
//     blanket fold. Only the big blind is left to act and the posted blind discounts the
//     raise, which makes it the widest opening seat at the table. The steal check is shared
//     with late position (isStealSpot), and it now requires an actually unopened pot rather
//     than the old "you can try a steal if it folded to you" hedge.
//
// Showdown verdicts graded at bet time, not at showdown
//   - A player who barrels air and then backs into a pair or two pair on a later street was
//     graded by their finished hand and came out as "Reasonable hand ran into better". Cards
//     that land after the last bet carried no decision, so they no longer earn a value label:
//     if the hand was air or a weak pair with no draw on every street the player bet, the
//     verdict is now CLEAR_BLUFF / BLUFF_WET and it counts toward their bluff rate.
//   - Genuine value lines are untouched — top pair, overpairs and real draws (semi-bluffs)
//     all fail the check. Wider than the existing GAMBLE_LOST rule, which only catches a
//     single bet of 90%+ of stack and misses players who get stacked across several streets.
//
// v6.4 (2026-07-30)
// -----------------
// Vs Me — head-to-head tab in the player panel
//   - New tab (non-self panels only) showing just the hands you actually played against
//     the player you opened, rather than every hand of theirs you happened to observe.
//     The History tab keeps its full observed-hands view untouched.
//   - Each card is the same History card plus a block for your own side of that hand:
//     your hole cards, made hand and position, whether you won/lost/folded, your
//     attributed chip result, and which of you forced the other to fold.
//   - Storage rides on the existing history entry — buildHistEntry now carries a vsHero
//     snapshot (hero's cards, position, entry action, result, how deep you both went in
//     the pot, the fold attribution). No new store, no new merge or migration path: the
//     entries dedupe by handId and pass unknown fields through as they always did.
//   - heroNet per hand reuses the same even-split attribution that already feeds
//     s.chipsVsHero, so per-hand figures and the lifetime total agree. Multiway pots
//     stay approximate for the same reason, and the pane says so.
//   - Depth filter (all / both put money in / saw the flop together / showdowns only)
//     plus its own JSON export. Lifetime-scoped across every stake on purpose: matchup
//     sample matters more here than matching the table you're currently sitting at.
//   - Hands recorded before this version have no vsHero and are simply left out, with a
//     note saying why instead of an empty pane. Heads-up hands are still skipped unless
//     "Heads-up tracking" is on — the pane points at that setting.
//   - Refactors: buildHistoryHtml's per-entry renderer extracted to buildHistEntryHtml so
//     both tabs render from one place; the self-cards/hand-scoring block extracted to
//     resolveShownHand() so hero's snapshot can be taken before the finalization loop
//     without a second copy of that logic; pinning now restyles every on-screen copy of
//     a hand instead of only the clicked button.
//
// v6.3 (2026-07-28)
// -----------------
// Quick Read — on-demand live read of one player's current hand
//   - New ⚡ button in the seat bottom row, left of the collusion flag. Click it for a
//     popover reading how that player is betting/calling THIS hand, judged against their
//     own tracked history. Works on every street.
//   - Deliberately no new poker math. buildLiveActionRead() assembles reads the coach
//     already computes but only fires on its own triggers (hero's turn, a specific logged
//     action): _villainSizingTierRead + buildSizingTierTell for preflop sizing,
//     getSizingTellNote for the current street's bet size, getOpponentLinePattern +
//     getPersonalLineExpectation + interpretLineDeviation for line-vs-baseline, and
//     _villainWeightedClasses for likely holdings. Each keeps its own sample gate, so a
//     thin-data player yields fewer rows rather than invented reads.
//   - The one addition on top of reuse: interpretLineDeviation() stays silent when a
//     player runs their standard line, which is right for an interrupt-driven coach but
//     wrong for a read you asked for — so the "true to form" case is filled in from the
//     same expectation object.
//   - Button is gated on hasLiveActionThisHand(): it appears only once the player has made
//     an actual decision. Posting a blind doesn't count, so it never shows up on a fresh
//     deal with nothing behind it, and never permanently widens a crowded mobile seat row.
//   - Popover re-renders on the existing 2s seat-sync tick so an open read tracks the hand
//     as it develops (scroll position preserved). Dismisses on outside click or Escape.
//   - "Full deep dive →" hands off to the companion Analyzer via the existing
//     tphud:openAnalyzer event, shown only when that script reports itself ready — this
//     file still never needs to know whether it's installed.
//   - Extracted positionFloatingPanel() from showTip() so the popover reuses the existing
//     anchor/flip placement math instead of carrying a second copy.
//   - buildLiveActionRead and hasLiveActionThisHand exposed on the analyzer bridge.
// Quick Read — board awareness and bluff-profile matching
//   - The read now looks at the cards on the table, not just the betting. _quickBoardRead()
//     runs the villain's sizing-filtered range through _rangeBoardSummary() (the existing
//     aggregation behind the range-story note) to get the weighted share of their range
//     that smashes / pairs / is live on a draw / missed outright, shown as bars plus the
//     board's own texture tags.
//   - Draw chase vs semi-bluff is split by what they actually did: a draw-heavy range that
//     checks or calls on a flushy/connected board reads as chasing, the same range betting
//     reads as a semi-bluff. Requires the board to genuinely have that draw live, so a high
//     drawPct on a dry board stays silent instead of inventing a chase.
//   - New _villainBluffRate() (sibling of _villainFoldVsBet) surfaces the card-verified
//     bluffCount/totalVerdicts rate. When they're the aggressor it's matched against the
//     board read and stated as a conjunction — "bluffs 34% of showdowns AND this board
//     misses their range" is a much stronger claim than either half, so the combined
//     wording only appears when both hold.
//   - Both gate on existing sample floors (beatBubbleMinSample for the range, 5 verdicts
//     for the bluff rate), so thin-data players get fewer rows rather than invented reads.
// Quick Read — conditional line history (replaces the vague aggression readout)
//   - "100% aggressive this hand vs 75% baseline" was true but useless: it never said
//     whether the aggression was value or a stab, which is the only thing the number is
//     there to help decide. _quickLineHistory() replaces it as the headline read.
//   - It filters the player's tracked history down to hands where he entered the pot the
//     same way AND ran the same street actions AND bet the same size bucket, then reports
//     what he actually turned up with (air / pair / real hand, over the subset where his
//     cards were revealed) and how those hands ended. So the limp-then-lead-flop example
//     now reads as "he does this 14 times, showed down 9, had nothing 5 of those, and won
//     it uncontested 8 of 14", which is an actual decision.
//   - Four-step fallback ladder when the exact spot is too rare: exact size, then any size
//     on the same line, then same pot entry only, then the street action alone. The level
//     that matched is reported in the wording ("counting at this size" vs "counting
//     whatever he did before") so a relaxed match never reads as a precise one. Below 4
//     matches at every level it returns nothing rather than guessing.
//   - Uncontested-win rate is called out when it is high, because that is the
//     reinforcement loop behind a habitual stab and the part a raw aggression number hides.
//   - Aggression is kept but demoted to a supporting line, only shown when the gap is 25pp
//     or more, and a single postflop decision is now labelled as noise instead of being
//     rendered as a confident "100% aggressive".
// Quick Read — wording pass
//   - All Quick Read strings now go through _voice() for both coach personalities, and were
//     rewritten to drop em dashes and clinical label prefixes per the house style. Line
//     descriptions go through _describeLine() so the internal "raise → bet" token form is
//     never surfaced; it says "limps in then bets the flop big" instead.
//
// v6.2 (2026-07-26)
// -----------------
// Collusion detection — re-tuned after going quiet
//   - The whipsaw fix (see v4.5 below) was tuned hard against false positives from
//     legit squeeze plays and ended up firing so rarely it's easy to forget the
//     feature exists. Dialed the frequency dial back up without touching the
//     false-positive guards themselves: non-faction whipsaw-only pairs now need
//     2+ events again (was 3+), and the non-faction soft-play commit threshold
//     dropped from 35% to 30%.
//   - Added faction "family" grouping: some factions split members across several
//     differently-named factions to dodge same-faction detection (e.g. SMTH -
//     Phoenix Nirvana / SMTH - High Pressure, Natural Selection 1 / 2).
//     sharesFaction() now also treats two players as same-faction if their
//     faction names match the same curated FACTION_FAMILIES pattern, on top of
//     the existing exact-faction-id check. Patterns are deliberately narrow
//     (anchored, specific) to avoid lumping together factions that just happen
//     to have similar names.
//   - The passive seat faction flag (badge highlighting shared faction — separate
//     from the collusion warning, doesn't require any suspicious event to have
//     happened) now uses the same family grouping via getFactionGroupKey(), so
//     it lights up for family members immediately, not just after a soft-play/
//     whipsaw event triggers the collusion tracker. This was the actual gap:
//     two SMTH sub-factions at the same table weren't sharing an exact faction
//     ID, so the flag never lit even though the family match was already wired
//     into the collusion event logic.
//
// v5.15 (2026-07-19)
// -----------------
// Bug fixes (found via a 3-agent review of the v5.14 additions)
//   - appendAutoTag() pinned s.history[0] AFTER its duplicate-tag guard, so a hand whose
//     autotag label+extra matched the immediately-preceding tag from an EARLIER hand (common
//     — several triggers always use extra:null) silently skipped pinning. Pin now happens
//     unconditionally before the guard's early return.
//   - s.chipsVsHero was the only per-opponent counter not skipped during heads-up hands —
//     could show P&L activity for an opponent with no matching handsObserved/history for
//     that hand. Now gated behind !isHU like every other per-opponent stat.
//   - The Analyzer's "show lost to" checkbox shared a hardcoded id with the live panel's copy
//     (harmless there since that listener is scoped to the panel element, but the Analyzer's
//     copy was simply dead). Analyzer now renames it and wires its own toggle.
// Live panel — deep-dive button + tilt banner
//   - New 🔎 header button (only shown once the companion Player Analyzer script reports
//     itself ready) dispatches a tphud:openAnalyzer event so the panel never has to know or
//     care whether that separate script is installed.
//   - computeTiltTrigger() (post-big-loss looseness/tightness read) moved out of the Analyzer
//     and into this file so both scripts share one definition; exposed via the bridge. Also
//     now surfaced live as a Stats-tab banner, no page-alt-tab required to see it.
// New tracking (small additions, no live-hand-flow changes)
//   - History entries now store position and flopPlayers (players who saw the flop) —
//     both were already computed live and discarded; the Analyzer can now build
//     position-conditioned and multi-way-vs-heads-up views post-hoc.
//   - s.shownHands[hand] now tracks threeBetCount/squeezeCount alongside the existing pfr
//     count, so shown-hand range views can split "what do they 3-bet/squeeze with" from
//     "what do they just open with."
// Companion script support
//   - exposeAnalyzerBridge() also exposes computeTiltTrigger and the TILT_BIG_LOSS_BB
//     threshold value.
//
// v5.14 (2026-07-19)
// -----------------
// Leaderboard — search, tier filter, more insight
//   - Search box filters by name/Torn ID. Tier filter buttons (Whale/Fish/Reg/
//     Regular/Unknown) with live counts. Added PFR% and AFq% columns and a
//     "Recent" sort using each player's lastSeen timestamp. Each row now shows
//     the same one-line style read the panel uses ("plays very loosely
//     pre-flop..."), extracted into a shared buildStyleSummary() helper.
// Range tab — search
//   - Both the self and opponent hand-range lists (Range tab) can now be
//     filtered by typing a hand, e.g. "AA" or "AK", instead of only sorting.
// History — bigger, pinnable
//   - Per-player History cap raised 30 → 100. Notable hands (autotagged plays,
//     pots over ~40 BB, or manually pinned via the new 📌 button) are exempt
//     from the rolling eviction, up to a 300-entry hard ceiling.
// New tracking
//   - All-in bets/raises are now cross-referenced against board texture
//     (postAllinWetCount / postAllinDryCount) and surfaced as a "Shove
//     Tendency" bar on the Stats tab (3+ all-ins needed to show).
//   - Rough per-opponent chip P&L vs hero (s.chipsVsHero): hero's net result
//     each hand is split evenly across whichever opponents didn't fold before
//     the hand's resolution. An approximation in multi-way pots by design —
//     there's no clean way to attribute a shared pot to one specific opponent.
//     Surfaced as a "Chips vs You" line on the Stats tab for opponents.
// Companion script support
//   - Exposed a read-only bridge (window.__tornPokerHUD_bridge) of the HUD's
