//
// Self profile — honest MIXED label at large samples
//   - "You Are: Unpredictable" with 50+ hands no longer claims "not enough
//     data yet". It now names the two archetypes your stats sit between and
//     the closest fit, since at that sample the blend is real, not noise.
//
// v5.5 (2026-07-08)
// -----------------
// Coach — raiser range-advantage read (fires with zero showdown history)
//   - When the preflop raiser bets postflop and there is no shown-hand history
//     to range them with, the coach falls back to theory: their assumed raising
//     range (sized from their real PFR when 10+ hands observed, generic sharp
//     range otherwise) is scored against the board. High boards → "K-high board
//     favors a raising range, their aggression is credible"; low connected
//     boards → "boards like this miss a raising range, less automatic respect".
//     Wide raisers self-correct: a 50% PFR range hits low boards, so no note.
//
// Coach — preflop range read shows up far more often
//   - Floor dropped from 4 sizing-weighted showdowns to 1: the read is purely
//     descriptive ("his raises at this size have shown KQo"), so even a single
//     size-matched showdown is worth surfacing. Thin samples are labelled
//     "(only N showdowns, thin sample)".
//   - Added the missing TPHUD-DEBUG console line explaining silence, cached
//     per hand/villain/size so it logs once per decision instead of every tick.
//
// v5.4 (2026-07-08)
// -----------------
// Coach — Torn-reality corrections to the range/blocker notes
//   - Fold-equity gate: the "good spot to bluff" note now checks the target's
//     fold-vs-flop-bet rate. Under 30% folds (5+ samples) the advice flips to
//     "their range missed but they don't fold, bet your made hands only".
//   - Survivorship-bias caveat: shownHands only contains hands that reached
//     showdown, so wide players' junk is invisible. When the villain's PFR is
//     30%+ (raiser) or VPIP 45%+ (caller) with 10+ hands, "range missed"
//     claims get a "treat this as a lean" qualifier instead of stating fact.
//   - Whale-call filter: a preflop call under ~3% of the caller's stack is
//     pocket change and carries no range info. Range reads on such calls are
//     suppressed (reason logged to console).
//   - Fold-vs-bet-size tracking (new data, fills over sessions): the biggest
//     bet a player faces postflop is bucketed by fraction of their stack
//     (<5% / 5-15% / 15%+) with fold-or-continue recorded. When someone calls
//     small but folds 65%+ to big bets, the coach adds "Sizing read: if you
//     bluff, size up".
//   - Straight blockers: on connected boards the wet-board warnings now say
//     which straights hero's hole ranks remove ("your T blocks 2 of 3 possible
//     straights"), mirroring the existing flush-blocker readout. Removed the
//     flush blockerNote string that was defined but never rendered.
//
// v5.3 (2026-07-07)
// -----------------
// Coach — blocker & range notes fire in both directions, not just when defending
//   - Attacking blocker note when facing a single open: big aces, suited wheel
//     aces and offsuit king-broadways are flagged as re-raise candidates (with
//     the why); suited broadways and small pairs get "this gains more as a
//     call". Premiums skipped, the chart already covers them. Vs loose openers
//     the bluff half of the advice is switched off.
//   - Preflop range read when facing a raise: lists what the raiser has
//     historically shown at this open size ("raises at ~5BB have shown AA, KK").
//   - Attack-mode range check when nobody has bet postflop: reads every active
//     opponent's sizing-filtered shown range against the board. Warns when the
//     board fits someone's history, flags a bluff spot only when everyone is
//     sampled and everyone missed. Skips 4+ way pots.
//   - Shared _rangeBoardSummary() feeds both facing- and attack-mode notes.
//
// v5.2 (2026-07-07)
// -----------------
// Coach — blocker & range-story notes
//   - Preflop blocker note when facing a 3-bet/4-bet (≥4BB): holding an A or K
//     tells you how many AA/KK/AK combos the re-raiser can still hold; low/mid
//     pocket pairs get the "blocks nothing, call to set mine" warning. Loose
//     opponents (maniac/fish) get a fold-equity caveat instead.
//   - Range story note when facing a postflop bet: checks the aggressor's
//     sizing-filtered shown-hand history (shownHands + BBx Gaussian weighting)
//     against the current board. Flags when the board smashes what they have
//     historically shown at this size, or when their shown range is all bricks
//     ("has this guy ever raised this size with low connectors?").
//   - Extracted _villainWeightedClasses() — shared by the beat bubble,
//     spectator ranges and the new range story (was duplicated inline twice).
//
// v4.5 (2026-04-24)
// -----------------
// Storage
//   - Migrated all persistent data (stats, live stacks, hand history, suspicion
//     pairs) from GM_setValue/localStorage to IndexedDB. No more quota errors,
//     works on every platform including TornPDA without a userscript manager.
//   - One-time automatic migration merges existing GM/localStorage data into IDB
//     on first load — no data loss. Per-player merge uses handsObserved as
//     tiebreaker so the richer record always wins.
//   - Settings and intro flag intentionally kept in localStorage (sync read
//     required at startup, no quota risk).
//   - Removed @grant GM_setValue and @grant GM_info (no longer used).
//     GM_getValue kept for the one-time migration read.
//
// Collusion detection — whipsaw fix
//   - Moved checkWhipsaw() from firing at the moment of the 3-bet to running at
//     hand finalisation where full action data is available.
//   - Added raiser-called check: only flags a whipsaw if the original raiser
//     called the 3-bet (soft play). Folder or 4-bettor = normal poker, skipped.
//   - Added preflopRaiseCount > 2 guard: a 4-bet from either party clears the
//     flag entirely.
//   - Victims must have actually folded preflop (squeezed out). Callers are no
//     longer counted as victims.
//   - Non-faction whipsaw-only pairs now require 3+ events (up from 2) before
//     showing the indicator.
//   - Result: aggressive 3-bettors and normal squeeze spots no longer trigger
//     false collusion alerts.
//
// Player name improvements
//   - Opponent names are now clickable links to their Torn profile
//     (https://www.torn.com/profiles.php?XID=...). Opens in a new tab.
//   - Clicking the HUD badge does not trigger the profile link (click on badge
//     is correctly isolated).
//   - Long names are scaled down to prevent truncation caused by the badge
//     taking space: 6-7 chars → 10px, 8-11 chars → 9px, 12+ chars → 8px.
//
// Help glossary
//   - Added "Icons & Indicators" section explaining every emoji and seat
//     indicator: 🎭 bluffer, 🎯 draw chaser, 💎 value player, 🃏 marginal
//     overplayer, 📞 loose caller, ▼/▽ stack drop, ! alert, ✎ auto-tag,
//     net worth pill, faction flag, and ⚠ collusion warning.
//
// Draw detection bug fix
//   - Fixed open-ended straight draw misclassification for A-high draws.
//     Holding AJ on a QQK board (J-Q-K-A, missing T) was incorrectly reported
//     as an open-ended straight draw. The Ace caps the top of the window so
//     only one card completes it — correctly reclassified as a gutshot.
//   - Fix applied to both findStraightDraw() (live coach) and detectDraw()
//     (verdict analysis) independently.
//
